 "voiceover": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Your NOT IN query returns zero rows?"
  },
  {
   "id": "bug",
   "text": "Most devs blame the data here."
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "But if the subquery has even one NULL, NOT IN compares against unknown, so every row gets filtered out."
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "text": "Use NOT EXISTS instead. It skips the NULL safely. Zero rows becomes every correct match."
  },
  {
   "id": "bait",
   "text": "Have you hit this NULL trap? Comment yes or no."
  },
  {
   "id": "follow",
   "text": "Follow K four coding for part four."
  }
